{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787089245058002001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"illiterate-alkylic-solenodon","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"57c889426a1c3721f25c3eedccea9efbcf7d5f584058ae4238d1c32370ea56e2","event_uuid":"b8563e0f-680e-4753-92fd-2a3808e14918","position":{"commit_sha":"aa24d4ef3f4b09ebd50c1231fb4ab008eda31bd6","position":"1787081169597662001-b8563e0f-680e-4753-92fd-2a3808e14918"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"68113c7e12a3d8bc6bc14374b44cf409820b4d8e1542d5f59de4c306310af1a3","event_uuid":"b9795988-082f-49a0-8524-351d63cd9fe6","position":{"commit_sha":"913ac80e03e38b104f211fbc20cbb2a9b33be9c4","position":"1787081181954666001-b9795988-082f-49a0-8524-351d63cd9fe6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"60530a42f14b97542d457a9ecbd5db928750ce683d249a185b76bbc17094d127","event_uuid":"0bdb8b6e-2c2a-4565-b340-ece553a9d106","position":{"commit_sha":"68b3d393ded5a214996a4f532f985f43f916025a","position":"1787081324974400001-0bdb8b6e-2c2a-4565-b340-ece553a9d106"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787081169597662001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0bdb8b6e-2c2a-4565-b340-ece553a9d106","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"60c1-80de-a22f-4d39"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe workflow editor currently presents authored YAML/BPMN configuration without a trustworthy view of the effective criteria policy derived from built-ins plus project overlays. RP-06 adds an immutable derived policy and an explicit project applicability rule; exposing derived state as if it were editable topology would create a second policy authority and make misconfiguration difficult to diagnose.\n\n## Approach\nExtend the workflow-editor server to obtain the S1 `CriteriaSnapshot` for the selected repository and expose a narrow, read-only Effective Policy view. Keep Authored Workflow as the only editable YAML/BPMN topology. The effective view shows snapshot digest/source, criterion id, gate, execution tier, effective posture/threshold, applicability summary, enabled/disabled state, and a concise derived reason. It never serializes edits back into workflow or project routing.\n\nAt authoring/save validation, a new `project.*` code-review LLM criterion must have a non-empty list of non-empty repository-relative `applies_to` globs. The editor rejects an empty/missing selector with the exact `[\"**\"]` repository-wide remedy. Built-in entries, project DET criteria, and plan-review criteria retain their distinct trigger authoring controls and are not forced through this field.\n\nKeep stored execution trace and per-call debugging detail out of the editor response. The Effective Policy panel is configuration provenance, not a review-result/status viewer. Repository or validation errors fail the save or mark the effective view unavailable with a located, actionable message; they do not silently display packaged defaults as effective policy.\n\n## Rationale and Compatibility\nA read-only projection makes the centralized pattern visible while preserving one authored source of topology. Older workflow files remain readable. The UI and server add fields without rewriting saved YAML/BPMN, and rollback removes the panel/endpoint while leaving authored artifacts unchanged.\n\n## Testing\nUse server contract tests with real overlay/snapshot compilation and focused editor DOM/state tests. The oracle is the serialized authored document remaining byte-equivalent while the read-only view changes with project policy. Negative controls cover built-in empty trigger semantics, project DET, and plan review. Error fixtures prove unavailable policy is explicit and save validation is fail-loud.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The editor renders distinct Authored Workflow and read-only Effective Policy sections, and no action in the effective section mutates or serializes YAML/BPMN.\n- [ ] Effective Policy data comes from the repository-bound `CriteriaSnapshot` and displays digest/source plus concise criterion gate, tier, posture, applicability, and enabled/disabled provenance.\n- [ ] Creating or saving a project code-review LLM criterion with missing, empty, non-list, or blank globs is refused with the criterion location and `use [\"**\"] for repository-wide` remedy.\n- [ ] Built-in secondary triggers, project DET selector controls, and plan-review `applies_at`/`trigger` authoring remain valid negative controls and are not subjected to the project-LLM glob rule.\n- [ ] A snapshot load/validation failure marks Effective Policy unavailable with an actionable located error and never substitutes packaged defaults or permits an invalid save.\n- [ ] Server and editor tests prove policy changes update only the derived view while authored workflow round-trips byte-equivalently.\n- [ ] Editor payloads contain no per-unit discovery trace, raw prompt/context body, provider response, or secret.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_server.py","reason":"Serve repository-bound effective-policy data and located validation errors."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_contracts.py","reason":"Define the narrow read-only effective-policy response contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx","reason":"Render separate authored and effective policy views plus the glob remedy."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_assets/dist/editor.js","reason":"Regenerated shipped editor bundle."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_editor_effective_policy.py","reason":"Server, read-only projection, unavailable state, and sensitive-field exclusion tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_editor_roundtrip.py","reason":"Authored YAML/BPMN byte-equivalent round-trip negative control."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_editor_batch.py","reason":"Project LLM glob authoring validation and built-in/DET/plan-review controls."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","60c1-80de-a22f-4d39"],["parent","58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp-06","llm","workflow-editor","ux"],"ticket_id":"65bf-173b-e16b-4bb9","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-06 S6 — Separate authored workflow from effective review policy","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b8563e0f-680e-4753-92fd-2a3808e14918","b9795988-082f-49a0-8524-351d63cd9fe6","0bdb8b6e-2c2a-4565-b340-ece553a9d106"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787089245058002001,"uuid":"85892f5c-899c-4257-9bc1-ffbebceae580"}